     "command": "cd <run>/work/R3/c/w && cat > groceries.csv <<'EOF'\nitem,cost_usd\nChicken breasts and thighs,40.00\nGround beef,28.00\nPork shoulder,22.00\nSalmon fillets,30.00\nEggs (4 dozen),18.00\nMilk and yogurt,32.00\nCheese,24.00\nButter,10.00\nFresh produce (weekly),120.00\nFrozen vegetables and fruit,20.00\n\"Rice, pasta, grains\",25.00\nBread and tortillas,20.00\n\"Canned tomatoes, beans, broth\",28.00\n\"Oils, spices, condiments\",25.00\nCereal and oats,15.00\nCoffee and tea,22.00\nSnacks,25.00\nDinner party: beef roast,60.00\nDinner party: cheese and charcuterie appetizers,35.00\nDinner party: salad and side dish produce,30.00\nDinner party: dessert ingredients,20.00\nDinner party: sparkling water and mixers,15.00\nDinner party: rolls,8.00\nEOF\ntotal=$(awk -F, 'NR>1{s+=$NF}END{printf \"%.2f\",s}' groceries.csv)\necho $total\ncat > meal-plan.md <<EOF\n# Monthly Meal Plan\n\n**Grocery budget limit used: \\$700 per month** (updated from the earlier \\$600 figure).\n\n- Estimated total in groceries.csv: \\$$total\n- Remaining buffer: \\$$(awk \"BEGIN{printf \\\"%.2f\\\", 700-$total}\")\n\n## Overview\n- Weekly dinners built around chicken, ground beef, pork shoulder, and salmon, plus rice/pasta/bean-based meals.\n- One dinner party (about 8 guests) mid-month: beef roast, cheese and charcuterie appetizers, salad and sides, dessert, and non-alcoholic drinks (\\$168 of the total).\n- Costs are rough estimates; adjust to local prices.\nEOF\ncat meal-plan.md",
